# The build-context ignore file for the ONE image this repository builds
# (docker/Dockerfile). A Dockerfile-adjacent
# `*.dockerignore` would SHADOW this file entirely
# (https://docs.docker.com/build/concepts/context — a Dockerfile-specific
# ignore-file takes precedence), so there is only this one — the FerroEHR shape.
#
# What the image BAKES therefore must not be excluded here: the runtime stage
# COPYs `artifacts/`, `specs/openehr/` and `party/` into /work (#420), because a
# record has to name a catalogue revision that belongs to a published release,
# and an instance that mounts nothing has no other way to read them. An
# exclusion of those trees fails that build, which is how it was found. The same
# holds for `registry/keys/registry-signing.pub.asc`, the public half /verify
# checks a published record against (#430), and for
# `deploy/hosted/docker-compose.yml` plus `deploy/hosted/Caddyfile`, the hosted
# posture the deploy extracts from the image it pulled (#423). Nothing below
# excludes `deploy/`, and nothing may start to.
#
# Everything else stays out, with ONE re-included directory: a smaller context
# keeps COPY layers stable across edits to what images never read, and
# excluding a tree the console compiles against breaks the from-source build
# with a missing-file error nothing else catches.
#
# What must NOT be excluded, so a future edit does not quietly break a build:
# `app/*/src/`, the manifests, `Cargo.lock`, `rust-toolchain.toml` (the builder stage
# compiles from them) and `bin/` (the CI target COPYs the prebuilt native binary
# from there).

# Build output. The single most important line: `target/` alone can be tens of
# gigabytes.
target/
**/target/

# History. It adds no compile input, and it invalidates the COPY layer on every
# commit and every fetch (https://docs.docker.com/build/cache). Build provenance
# comes from the OCI-standard REVISION build-arg instead, which the publishing
# workflow sets.
.git/
.gitattributes

# The published schemas, the verification pack and the brand assets — read by
# no image. The catalogue (artifacts/), the vendored oracle (specs/) and the
# party declarations (party/) are NOT listed: the hosted overlay bakes them
# (header above), and the operator image simply never COPYs them.
#
# `assets/brand/` is the one exception, because it is a COMPILE input twice
# over: the console's `public/` entries are symlinks into it, and its export
# module reads the seal-card master through `include_str!`. Excluding it fails
# the builder stage (https://docs.docker.com/build/concepts/context — a `!`
# line re-includes a path an earlier pattern excluded).
schemas/
verification-pack/
assets/
!assets/brand/

# Tests and their fixtures: nothing in the image runs them.
app/veredictum/tests/

# The fuzzing workspace: its own nightly workspace, never a compile input for
# the image. `**/target/` above already drops its 4 GB target tree; this line
# drops the ~80 MB corpus and seeds, whose weekly churn would otherwise
# invalidate the COPY layer on every campaign.
fuzz/

# The documentation site: rendered by its own workflow, read by nothing the
# image compiles.
website/

# CI, tooling, agent and editor directories — never a compile input.
.github/
.githooks/
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local environment, secrets, coverage and logs. The secret patterns mirror
# `.gitignore`: an IXIT declaration carries a live endpoint and its credentials,
# and SECURITY.md treats leaking one as a vulnerability in this instrument.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.log
ixit.local.json
**/ixit.local.json
lcov.info
*.profraw
coverage/
.sccache/
.DS_Store
